// Eternit lane 11 - Labyrinth. All walls traced from the official drawing (NormMiniatur S 12, Bahn 11), rendered from
// the PDF at 10x and scaled with the 90 cm lane width (1 px = 1.24 mm, so about +-1 cm). Lane +x = the player's right.
// OFFICIAL: the lane rises from 60-100 cm behind the lane start (using 80) to the lane end; entrances 12-20 cm wide;
//   with four entrances only the 2nd from the right leads to the target, the others must not lead to it. The black bars in
//   the drawing are flat strips across the tops of the walls, not blocks - all four entrances are open underneath; target = the area between the parallel walls in the centre, with or without a hole; no Grenzlinie.
// FROM THE DRAWING: wings from the Banden; an outer ring (r about 62 cm) with a small wedge at the back; a pear-shaped
//   middle ring (r about 43 cm) that carries a short lip at the back; a pear-shaped inner loop (r about 23 cm) that is
//   open at the back for 7 cm; behind that opening the target pocket, closed towards the tee (7.5 cm wide in the
//   drawing; built 14 cm wide with a hole, see FROM PHOTOS).
// Thin bracing rods across the wall tops as in the drawing and the Neuwied photo (the ball passes underneath).
// ESTIMATES: wall height 10 cm (side view of the drawing and photos, +-25 %); lane end 40 cm above the tee (side view
//   and photos, +-25 %).
// FROM PHOTOS (Uppsala, Rothe insert, DMV booklet): the target is a U-shaped pocket about one and a half hole
//   diameters wide with a hole (the norm allows it with or without hole; its drawing shows a 7.5 cm box); flat strips
//   lie across the tops of the entrance walls and brace the rings; walls about 10 cm high.
// The lip of the middle ring is carried on to the inner loop (as in the Uppsala, Rothe and minigolfbau photos), so a ball
//   from the second entrance from the left cannot reach the target; the opening of the inner loop is about 9 cm (drawing).
